name w3-04-weasels-leave-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - PACKAGE Q FAILURE MODE 2: THE WEASELS LEAVE EARLY.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w3-03-weasel-close.fbm. THE ONE THING THAT DIFFERS is the SEAD pair's position relative to
# the package - its `spawn` longitude and its first `wp`, four numbers that express one fact. Everything
# else, including the strikers' entire sortie, the battery, the net and the clock, is the control's.
#
# WHY THAT IS THE LEVER, AND WHAT IT COSTS TO SAY SO HONESTLY. The anchor's Weasels left ON FUEL [T4].
# FlightBox has no aerial refuelling, no external tank and no fuel-driven return-to-base (gap C5), and
# `FBPilot` reads fuel at exactly ONE place - the recovery out of a defensive break, which a SEAD pass
# never enters (sortie 06 measures that place). So a fuel-driven departure CANNOT be declared, and the
# campaign does not pretend otherwise: what is declared is the CONSEQUENCE the anchor cared about -
# the suppression element is not where the package needs it, and its shot is taken from a range at
# which the round does not arrive. The direction of the substitution is stated: this is a WEAKER claim
# than the anchor's, because a departed Weasel is also a Weasel that is no longer a target, and this
# file's own measurement shows that being a target was the larger half of its value.
#
# THE ARENA, the net-as-buried-cable, the substitutions (F-4G -> F-16CJ; no catalogue row as a
# combatant; ZSU-23-4 for 100 mm AAA), the time separation of the two engagements and what NIGHT is
# worth are stated in w3-03-weasel-close.fbm and hold unchanged.
# WHICH DEFENSIVE LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the MISSILE layer. No fighter flies in 03, 04 or 05.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: DOES THE STRIKE'S LOSS RATE CHANGE WHEN ITS COVER IS NOT THERE?
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint c0eff8b98797bab1), AND THE ANSWER IS NO - FOR A REASON THAT IS NOT IN THE SPEC:
#   the shots         both AGM-88 away at t = 8.4 / 23.3 from 42 km - both weasels shoot here and only
#                     the lead does in the control. Both rounds fall SHORT: ground impact at 44.0871 and
#                     44.1219 against a battery at 44.2000, i.e. 10.5 km and 7.3 km short. The round's
#                     reach on this geometry is bracketed between 20 km (the control: a 2.8 mm hit) and
#                     42 km (here: 10 km short), and that bracket IS the measurement
#   the battery       ALIVE, and it empties its whole magazine anyway: four V-601 at t = 122.2 .. 158.3,
#                     all four at the DEPARTING WEASELS (28.0, 27.3, 20.5, 19.9 km, brgDeg 277-280),
#                     `site GO_DARK why="magazine empty"` at t = 158.3. Two of the four end
#                     `stall/mush` in a tail chase they cannot win
#   the objective     `mission SUPPRESSION_LOST ... emittingS=120.1 allowanceS=120` at t = 120.1 - the
#                     allowance runs out while the battery is still on the air, which is what an
#                     unsuppressed position looks like in the verdict vocabulary
#   the strikers      2 of 2 released (t = 275.2 / 290.6), `q4tgt` DESTROYED - the same tick, the same
#                     miss distance and the same verdict as the control
# SO THE WEASEL THAT SHOT SHORT STILL SUPPRESSED THE BATTERY, by being the nearest firm track in its
# envelope while the strikers were still 40 km out. A FlightBox battery has no IFF interrogator and no
# threat priority; it engages what it can reach. THE COVER'S VALUE IS NOT ONLY ITS MISSILE.
#
# THAT RESULT HAS TWO POSSIBLE CAUSES AND THEREFORE GETS A CONTROL RUN (rule 4), NOT AN ARGUMENT.
# ATTRIBUTION RUN A2 is this geometry with the SEAD pair DELETED - the package with no suppression
# element at all, which is what the anchor actually describes. Its numbers are in
# doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md, State, and they are the other half of this file's answer.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      the two `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE mode=arm` lines and then `UNIT_RESULT
#                   unit=q4wsa_agm88_1 result=IMPACT ... lon=44.087` - a round that hit dirt, not a site;
#                   the four `site LAUNCH ... brgDeg=277..280` (west = the departing pair);
#                   `site GO_DARK why="magazine empty"`
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is expected and is not the measurement. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE TRIPLE
# (strikers that reached release, `site LAUNCH` count and WHO they were aimed at, `UNIT_RESULT
# unit=q4sa3`), read beside w3-03, w3-05 and attribution run A2. A reader who reports only "the target
# died in both files" has read the sortie backwards.

net kari4
  control q4nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member q4nod
  member q4sa3 autonomy free
  member q4flk autonomy free

unit q4wsa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws4 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.75000 5000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class fire_control
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.20000 43.82000 5000 480
  wp 33.20000 43.40000 5000 480
  objective suppress unit q4sa3 emitting 120
  objective survive

